{"jobs":[{"id":"1be7e643-cae8-4270-b998-f01d8d8e0389","title":"Software Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"NYC","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T13:54:36.640+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/1be7e643-cae8-4270-b998-f01d8d8e0389","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/1be7e643-cae8-4270-b998-f01d8d8e0389/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.silnahealth.com\">Silna Health</a> streamlines securing treatment approvals from health insurers. Our cutting-edge technology ensures faster access to care, reduced administrative burden for clinical staff, and timely payments for providers. Based in NYC, we partner with healthcare providers nationwide and are well funded by top-tier VCs.<br /></p><h2><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic intellectual curiosity, specifically as it pertains to software. You should like computers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backend experience.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Description</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Silna scales our technology platform to a broader customer base, we are expanding on a few efforts:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical case management.</strong> At times insurance companies require clinician action, and we’re pulling an email based process into a proper case management system, streamlining the clinical staff's processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>An external facing API.</strong> As our customers are leveraging Silna to automate never before automated processes, we have the opportunity to be the standard bearer for the proper data schema for prior authorizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Integrating cutting edge models</strong> into our automation processes. We are integrating new technologies such as OpenAI’s end to end voice model to automate tedious phone calls and Anthropic’s computer use model to automate traditional web portals.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">These are just a few of the engineering challenges we are presently tackling, and with healthcare being a relatively greenfield space, there’s constantly room to leverage software to 10x efficiency across clinical staff to the back office. We are bringing on engineers to help us execute across the board. This role reports directly into Silna’s CTO.</p><h2><strong>You’ll be great for this role if you:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Are focused on the problem instead of the technology. </strong>We’re not doing cutting edge AI research, we’re leveraging new technologies and applying them to critical healthcare workflows. Doing so effectively requires deep understanding, genuine curiosity, and deep empathy for the patient and clinical staff.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enjoy working in a high speed collaborative environment.</strong> If you like being given a Jira board and left alone in the corner, Silna isn’t the right place for you. We’re entirely in person, and each engineer maintains context on what one another is working on. We look for ways we can collaborate and leverage shared solutions for similar engineering problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Appreciate autonomy, agency, and accountability.</strong> Every engineer here is tasked with business outcomes, not a list of tickets. You’ll be working directly with the CTO and COO to strategize on how software can solve business problems, and you’ll be expected to translate customer needs into delivered software.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Tech Stack</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backend is a Flask app connected to a Postgres database, containerized and deployed leveraging ECS</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Frontend is a Next app statically built, deployed using s3 + Cloudfront</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We focus on simplicity in our technology stack so we can focus on the complexity of our customer's problems<br /></p>","descriptionPlain":"Silna Health https://www.silnahealth.com streamlines securing treatment approvals from health insurers. Our cutting-edge technology ensures faster access to care, reduced administrative burden for clinical staff, and timely payments for providers. Based in NYC, we partner with healthcare providers nationwide and are well funded by top-tier VCs.\n\n\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Authentic intellectual curiosity, specifically as it pertains to software. You should like computers.\n\n - Backend experience.\n\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\nAs Silna scales our technology platform to a broader customer base, we are expanding on a few efforts:\n\n - Clinical case management. At times insurance companies require clinician action, and we’re pulling an email based process into a proper case management system, streamlining the clinical staff's processes.\n\n - An external facing API. As our customers are leveraging Silna to automate never before automated processes, we have the opportunity to be the standard bearer for the proper data schema for prior authorizations.\n\n - Integrating cutting edge models into our automation processes. We are integrating new technologies such as OpenAI’s end to end voice model to automate tedious phone calls and Anthropic’s computer use model to automate traditional web portals.\n\nThese are just a few of the engineering challenges we are presently tackling, and with healthcare being a relatively greenfield space, there’s constantly room to leverage software to 10x efficiency across clinical staff to the back office. We are bringing on engineers to help us execute across the board. This role reports directly into Silna’s CTO.\n\n\nYOU’LL BE GREAT FOR THIS ROLE IF YOU:\n\n - Are focused on the problem instead of the technology. We’re not doing cutting edge AI research, we’re leveraging new technologies and applying them to critical healthcare workflows. Doing so effectively requires deep understanding, genuine curiosity, and deep empathy for the patient and clinical staff.\n\n - Enjoy working in a high speed collaborative environment. If you like being given a Jira board and left alone in the corner, Silna isn’t the right place for you. We’re entirely in person, and each engineer maintains context on what one another is working on. We look for ways we can collaborate and leverage shared solutions for similar engineering problems.\n\n - Appreciate autonomy, agency, and accountability. Every engineer here is tasked with business outcomes, not a list of tickets. You’ll be working directly with the CTO and COO to strategize on how software can solve business problems, and you’ll be expected to translate customer needs into delivered software.\n\n\nTECH STACK\n\nBackend is a Flask app connected to a Postgres database, containerized and deployed leveraging ECS\n\nFrontend is a Next app statically built, deployed using s3 + Cloudfront\n\nWe focus on simplicity in our technology stack so we can focus on the complexity of our customer's problems\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$130K – $215K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$130K - $215K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c8a33512-6d07-4da6-b04a-94b91f6ecb5e","tierSummary":"$130K – $215K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"70d4377c-d5f7-4a20-9bf7-80135ce57573","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"13bec0f6-0f45-475a-8dfa-8896e960ed0b","summary":"$130K – $215K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":130000,"maxValue":215000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":130000,"maxValue":215000}]}},{"id":"ff0fc433-fc26-4237-ba3d-086357b2475a","title":"Operations","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"NYC","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-23T20:33:50.358+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/ff0fc433-fc26-4237-ba3d-086357b2475a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/ff0fc433-fc26-4237-ba3d-086357b2475a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Operations at </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.silnahealth.com\"><strong>Silna</strong></a></h1><h2></h2><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Silna experiences explosive growth, we're seeking a talented Operations hire to join our team in NYC. Operations is core to Silna, and the notoriously opaque world of insurance operations needs someone who can build and optimize the processes that make everything run seamlessly. This role offers the chance to work hands-on, design workflows that matter, and drive real-world impact from day one—all while collaborating closely across our lean, high-performing team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an early member of our Operations team, you'll work on transforming complex insurance workflows into streamlined, scalable operations. One one side, you'll create SOPs that set our team of insurance specialists up for success while supporting our expansion across states, payers, and specialties. You'll also work closely and have the opportunity to manage our specialist teams, partner with engineering on automation opportunities by applying AI to solve real world problems. This is a unique chance to play a pivotal role in shaping the future of our business and the lives we touch, all within a data-first, startup environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><h3><strong>Complex Problem Solving, Process Design, &amp; Optimization</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and optimize core workflows for eligibility checks, benefit verifications, and prior authorizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with engineering to identify areas of opportunity for automation in operational processes, and use cutting-edge technology and apply AI-first solutions to automate key workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create SOPs that ensure consistent, accurate task completion across our operations team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Configure rules and frameworks for accomplishing tasks both automatically and manually</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Cross-Functional Leadership</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead our team of insurance specialists, providing guidance and ensuring operational excellence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with engineering to identify automation opportunities and design scalable systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product, engineering, and sales teams to align on goals and achieve shared outcomes</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Data &amp; Systems Thinking</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build robust tracking systems that provide visibility into operational performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze data to develop strategies for accelerating progress and achieving team OKRs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify areas for improvement and drive execution of solutions that address core business challenges</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What Sets You Apart</strong></h2><h3><strong>Experience &amp; Skills</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1-4+ years of experience in operations, consulting, or related fields—experience with insurance workflows or healthcare operations is a plus but not necessary</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to drive outcomes in complex and ambiguous environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience creating processes that scale with growing organizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project management skills with a track record of leading initiatives from concept to execution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data-driven approach with ability to analyze workflows and identify inefficiencies</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Character &amp; Mindset</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Self-starter</strong> who thrives in ambiguity and is comfortable navigating the complexity of insurance processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems thinker</strong> with a passion for automating and scaling solutions to simplify insurance-related challenges</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborative</strong> by nature, working effectively across small teams to achieve shared goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Detail-oriented</strong> with a focus on operational excellence and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Solution-oriented</strong> with the ability to design solutions that deliver tangible results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-driven</strong> with genuine care about making a difference in the lives of providers and patients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About Silna</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why Join Silna</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ground-floor opportunity to build foundational operations at a rapidly growing startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with the founding team and influence company direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation package including equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Chance to make a meaningful impact on healthcare delivery through operational excellence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fast-paced, dynamic environment that rewards initiative and results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to solve complex problems alongside brilliant colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is perfect for someone who loves building systems from scratch, thrives in fast-paced environments, and wants to be instrumental in transforming how healthcare providers interact with insurance. If you're ready to join a mission-driven company that's revolutionizing healthcare administration through operational excellence, we want to talk to you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A rapid-paced work environment with an incredibly enthusiastic and motivated team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The opportunity to work with customers that actually love the product</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to work on technology that is materially improving health outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation and benefits package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is fully in-person 5 days a week in our New York City office.</p>","descriptionPlain":"OPERATIONS AT SILNA https://www.silnahealth.com\n\n\n\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\nAs Silna experiences explosive growth, we're seeking a talented Operations hire to join our team in NYC. Operations is core to Silna, and the notoriously opaque world of insurance operations needs someone who can build and optimize the processes that make everything run seamlessly. This role offers the chance to work hands-on, design workflows that matter, and drive real-world impact from day one—all while collaborating closely across our lean, high-performing team.\n\nAs an early member of our Operations team, you'll work on transforming complex insurance workflows into streamlined, scalable operations. One one side, you'll create SOPs that set our team of insurance specialists up for success while supporting our expansion across states, payers, and specialties. You'll also work closely and have the opportunity to manage our specialist teams, partner with engineering on automation opportunities by applying AI to solve real world problems. This is a unique chance to play a pivotal role in shaping the future of our business and the lives we touch, all within a data-first, startup environment.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n\nCOMPLEX PROBLEM SOLVING, PROCESS DESIGN, & OPTIMIZATION\n\n - Design and optimize core workflows for eligibility checks, benefit verifications, and prior authorizations\n\n - Work with engineering to identify areas of opportunity for automation in operational processes, and use cutting-edge technology and apply AI-first solutions to automate key workflows\n\n - Create SOPs that ensure consistent, accurate task completion across our operations team\n\n - Configure rules and frameworks for accomplishing tasks both automatically and manually\n\n\nCROSS-FUNCTIONAL LEADERSHIP\n\n - Lead our team of insurance specialists, providing guidance and ensuring operational excellence\n\n - Partner with engineering to identify automation opportunities and design scalable systems\n\n - Collaborate with product, engineering, and sales teams to align on goals and achieve shared outcomes\n\n\nDATA & SYSTEMS THINKING\n\n - Build robust tracking systems that provide visibility into operational performance\n\n - Analyze data to develop strategies for accelerating progress and achieving team OKRs\n\n - Identify areas for improvement and drive execution of solutions that address core business challenges\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT SETS YOU APART\n\n\nEXPERIENCE & SKILLS\n\n - 1-4+ years of experience in operations, consulting, or related fields—experience with insurance workflows or healthcare operations is a plus but not necessary\n\n - Demonstrated ability to drive outcomes in complex and ambiguous environments\n\n - Strong experience creating processes that scale with growing organizations\n\n - Project management skills with a track record of leading initiatives from concept to execution\n\n - Data-driven approach with ability to analyze workflows and identify inefficiencies\n\n\nCHARACTER & MINDSET\n\n - Self-starter who thrives in ambiguity and is comfortable navigating the complexity of insurance processes\n\n - Systems thinker with a passion for automating and scaling solutions to simplify insurance-related challenges\n\n - Collaborative by nature, working effectively across small teams to achieve shared goals\n\n - Detail-oriented with a focus on operational excellence and accuracy\n\n - Solution-oriented with the ability to design solutions that deliver tangible results\n\n - Mission-driven with genuine care about making a difference in the lives of providers and patients\n\n\n\n\nABOUT SILNA\n\nHealthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.\n\nSilna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.\n\nWe work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.\n\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN SILNA\n\n - Ground-floor opportunity to build foundational operations at a rapidly growing startup\n\n - Work directly with the founding team and influence company direction\n\n - Competitive compensation package including equity\n\n - Chance to make a meaningful impact on healthcare delivery through operational excellence\n\n - Fast-paced, dynamic environment that rewards initiative and results\n\n - Opportunity to solve complex problems alongside brilliant colleagues\n\nThis role is perfect for someone who loves building systems from scratch, thrives in fast-paced environments, and wants to be instrumental in transforming how healthcare providers interact with insurance. If you're ready to join a mission-driven company that's revolutionizing healthcare administration through operational excellence, we want to talk to you.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A rapid-paced work environment with an incredibly enthusiastic and motivated team\n\n - The opportunity to work with customers that actually love the product\n\n - The ability to work on technology that is materially improving health outcomes\n\n - Competitive compensation and benefits package\n\n - 401k\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n   \n   \n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis role is fully in-person 5 days a week in our New York City office.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $185K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $185K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"482bb958-4669-4b19-b2a0-1b8cdda5bfd1","tierSummary":"$120K – $185K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"29f8753a-ffa7-4804-89ef-6c66ed27cdcd","summary":"$120K – $185K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":185000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":185000}]}},{"id":"01f88949-0d21-4f6e-93c1-e3ec364093ab","title":"ABA Authorization Specialist","department":"Operations Specialists","team":"Operations Specialists","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-17T18:08:12.775+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/01f88949-0d21-4f6e-93c1-e3ec364093ab","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/01f88949-0d21-4f6e-93c1-e3ec364093ab/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Silna</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna is looking for an enterprising prior authorization and benefits verifications expert to work closely with our customers - ABA (Autism), Mental Health, IOP, and Psych Testing providers - and complete these administrative tasks on their behalf. This is a unique role, as you will also be working closely with the Silna Product team to automate parts of the verification and authorization processes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with ABA / behavioral health providers and their billing teams to collect accurate patient information and communicate authorization decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with insurers to verify patient eligibility and benefits, and expediently complete prior authorizations using insurance portals or calling insurers directly. Ensure authorization is approved in a timeline manner by following up with insurers and providing additional information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be responsible for handling multiple prior authorizations simultaneously and create process to ensure top of the line performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand ABA- and other behavioral health-specific workflows, including creating treatment plans, re-authorization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Become a subject matter expert in behavioral health prior authorization workflows for large insurers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Silna Product/Engineering teams to share learnings about the prior authorization process to help automate parts of it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate effectively across multiple stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be willing to work 40 hours per week</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">​​<strong>Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate will have a strong understanding of insurance policies and ABA billing processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience completing prior authorizations for ABA <em>(preferred)</em> or other behavioral health services. Strong understanding of benefits including deductibles, co-insurance, out of pocket and benefits exclusions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have familiarity with payor portals and experience calling payors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have a strong work ethic: operate with urgency, work independently, be highly organized, detailed oriented and multi-task effectively</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have: Be familiar with providers software, including Electronic Medical Record Systems (EMR/EHR) like CentralReach and Rethink</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An highly competitive hourly rate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Chance to move from contractor to a well compensated full time position, which includes benefits and equity in the company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Best of all, a chance to make an impact on patients ability to access care</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please attach a resume and any other relevant details about your background. Please do not apply if you don't have the criteria required.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Type: Full-Time</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior Authorization (services, not medication): 2 years (Required)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ABA/Autism or other Behavioral Health prior authorization: 2 years (Required)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Insurance verification: 2 year (Required)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work Location: Remote</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT SILNA\n\nHealthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.\n\nSilna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.\n\nWe work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.\n\n\n\nAbout the Role\n\nSilna is looking for an enterprising prior authorization and benefits verifications expert to work closely with our customers - ABA (Autism), Mental Health, IOP, and Psych Testing providers - and complete these administrative tasks on their behalf. This is a unique role, as you will also be working closely with the Silna Product team to automate parts of the verification and authorization processes.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n - Work closely with ABA / behavioral health providers and their billing teams to collect accurate patient information and communicate authorization decisions\n\n - Work with insurers to verify patient eligibility and benefits, and expediently complete prior authorizations using insurance portals or calling insurers directly. Ensure authorization is approved in a timeline manner by following up with insurers and providing additional information\n\n - Be responsible for handling multiple prior authorizations simultaneously and create process to ensure top of the line performance\n\n - Understand ABA- and other behavioral health-specific workflows, including creating treatment plans, re-authorization\n\n - Become a subject matter expert in behavioral health prior authorization workflows for large insurers\n\n - Work closely with Silna Product/Engineering teams to share learnings about the prior authorization process to help automate parts of it\n\n - Communicate effectively across multiple stakeholders\n\n - Be willing to work 40 hours per week\n\nQualifications\n\n - The ideal candidate will have a strong understanding of insurance policies and ABA billing processes\n\n - 2+ years of experience completing prior authorizations for ABA (preferred) or other behavioral health services. Strong understanding of benefits including deductibles, co-insurance, out of pocket and benefits exclusions\n\n - Have familiarity with payor portals and experience calling payors\n\n - Have a strong work ethic: operate with urgency, work independently, be highly organized, detailed oriented and multi-task effectively\n\n - Nice to have: Be familiar with providers software, including Electronic Medical Record Systems (EMR/EHR) like CentralReach and Rethink\n\nBenefits\n\n - An highly competitive hourly rate\n\n - Chance to move from contractor to a well compensated full time position, which includes benefits and equity in the company\n\n - Remote role\n\n - Best of all, a chance to make an impact on patients ability to access care\n\nTo apply, please attach a resume and any other relevant details about your background. Please do not apply if you don't have the criteria required.\n\nJob Type: Full-Time\n\nExperience:\n\n - Prior Authorization (services, not medication): 2 years (Required)\n\n - ABA/Autism or other Behavioral Health prior authorization: 2 years (Required)\n\n - Insurance verification: 2 year (Required)\n\nWork Location: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$26 – $28 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"57c0e988-6825-4d49-a37c-2f81ee4346e4","tierSummary":"$26 – $28 per hour","title":"Base Salary","additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e1cacfd1-3566-49ae-a2bb-91f7c0dbcc2b","summary":"$26 – $28 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":26,"maxValue":28}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":26,"maxValue":28}]}},{"id":"38afa947-28c8-423f-953f-22ef7a680460","title":"Authorization and Verification Research Specialist","department":"Operations Specialists","team":"Operations Specialists","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-27T01:06:03.081+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/38afa947-28c8-423f-953f-22ef7a680460","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/38afa947-28c8-423f-953f-22ef7a680460/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Authorization and Verification Research Specialist</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote | Full time | 40 hours/week</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a detail-oriented insurance verification and prior authorization expert who thrives on research and problem-solving. In this role, you'll investigate payor requirements across insurance plans—digging into portals, policy updates, and submission processes—to uncover the specific steps needed to successfully submit prior authorizations and verify benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be our go-to researcher for understanding how different payors work, what documents they require, and how their processes vary across specialties. Your findings will directly enable our team to support healthcare providers and help patients access the care they need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is ideal for someone who loves the investigative side of insurance work, stays current on payor policy changes, and wants to build expertise across a wide range of insurance plans.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and document prior authorization and benefit verification requirements across diverse payors (commercial plans, state Medicaid programs, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate payor-specific submission processes: required documents, portals, fax numbers, CPT code requirements, and policy updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay informed on payor policy changes, especially those affecting authorization processes and benefit structures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate payor websites, newsletters, and representative communications to gather accurate, up-to-date information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate information from multiple sources and determine credibility of payor guidance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work independently to solve ambiguous problems where established processes don't yet exist</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate findings clearly to cross-functional stakeholders and adapt quickly to feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle tight deadlines and shifting priorities in a fast-paced startup environment</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong> Prior authorization and/or insurance verification experience at a healthcare clinic </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with payor submission processes and how requirements vary across different insurance plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong research skills and comfort navigating payor portals, websites, and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional attention to detail and ability to spot common authorization mistakes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with multiple payors and understanding process variations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to build or improve processes when protocols don't exist</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resilient problem-solver who thrives in ambiguous, evolving environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and comfort asking for help when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humility and willingness to learn from mistakes</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About Silna</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pay:</strong> $25-27/hour</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hours:</strong> 40 hours/week</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All necessary devices and system access provided</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Start date:</strong> ASAP</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Join Silna Health?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of a startup transforming healthcare administration. Your research will directly impact patients' ability to access timely care by helping providers navigate complex insurance requirements more effectively.</p>","descriptionPlain":"AUTHORIZATION AND VERIFICATION RESEARCH SPECIALIST\n\nRemote | Full time | 40 hours/week\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe're looking for a detail-oriented insurance verification and prior authorization expert who thrives on research and problem-solving. In this role, you'll investigate payor requirements across insurance plans—digging into portals, policy updates, and submission processes—to uncover the specific steps needed to successfully submit prior authorizations and verify benefits.\n\nYou'll be our go-to researcher for understanding how different payors work, what documents they require, and how their processes vary across specialties. Your findings will directly enable our team to support healthcare providers and help patients access the care they need.\n\nThis role is ideal for someone who loves the investigative side of insurance work, stays current on payor policy changes, and wants to build expertise across a wide range of insurance plans.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Research and document prior authorization and benefit verification requirements across diverse payors (commercial plans, state Medicaid programs, etc.)\n\n - Investigate payor-specific submission processes: required documents, portals, fax numbers, CPT code requirements, and policy updates\n\n - Stay informed on payor policy changes, especially those affecting authorization processes and benefit structures\n\n - Navigate payor websites, newsletters, and representative communications to gather accurate, up-to-date information\n\n - Validate information from multiple sources and determine credibility of payor guidance\n\n - Work independently to solve ambiguous problems where established processes don't yet exist\n\n - Communicate findings clearly to cross-functional stakeholders and adapt quickly to feedback\n\n - Handle tight deadlines and shifting priorities in a fast-paced startup environment\n   \n   \n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Required: Prior authorization and/or insurance verification experience at a healthcare clinic \n\n - Deep familiarity with payor submission processes and how requirements vary across different insurance plans\n\n - Strong research skills and comfort navigating payor portals, websites, and documentation\n\n - Exceptional attention to detail and ability to spot common authorization mistakes\n\n - Experience working with multiple payors and understanding process variations\n\n - Demonstrated ability to build or improve processes when protocols don't exist\n\n - Resilient problem-solver who thrives in ambiguous, evolving environments\n\n - Strong communication skills and comfort asking for help when needed\n\n - Humility and willingness to learn from mistakes\n\n\n\n\nABOUT SILNA\n\nHealthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.\n\nSilna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.\n\nWe work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION & BENEFITS\n\n - Pay: $25-27/hour\n\n - Hours: 40 hours/week\n\n - Fully remote\n\n - All necessary devices and system access provided\n\n - Start date: ASAP\n   \n   \n\nWhy Join Silna Health?\n\nBe part of a startup transforming healthcare administration. Your research will directly impact patients' ability to access timely care by helping providers navigate complex insurance requirements more effectively.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$26 – $28 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"76ec5bb5-8d2e-4843-954f-379d6b3ee298","tierSummary":"$26 – $28 per hour","title":"Base Salary","additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f79cc835-83ea-4f98-b6e7-6304bcea0a92","summary":"$26 – $28 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":26,"maxValue":28}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":26,"maxValue":28}]}},{"id":"f9c1519d-64be-4560-86a5-4e972e6cac5e","title":"Enterprise Account Executive","department":"GTM","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"NYC","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-23T14:49:12.804+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/f9c1519d-64be-4560-86a5-4e972e6cac5e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/f9c1519d-64be-4560-86a5-4e972e6cac5e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Enterprise Account Executive at </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.silnahealth.com\"><strong>Silna</strong></a></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Silna experiences explosive growth, we're seeking a top-tier Enterprise Account Executive to join our team in NYC. This is a ground-floor opportunity to shape our enterprise sales function and drive significant impact as we transform how healthcare providers clear patients for care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting directly to the CEO, you'll manage the full sales cycle for enterprise accounts, develop and execute strategic sales plans, and contribute to defining our go-to-market strategy. This role demands someone who thrives in ambiguity, builds exceptional relationships, and approaches sales with strategic sophistication.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><h3><strong>Sales Execution &amp; Strategy</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full sales cycle from prospecting to closing enterprise deals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and execute territory plans to achieve and exceed quota</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and deliver compelling presentations tailored to each prospect's unique challenges</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate complex buying committees and build consensus among multiple stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Negotiate contracts and strategic partnerships to maximize value</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify patterns and opportunities in the market before competitors</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Relationship Building</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cultivate relationships with C-level executives and key decision makers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a strong internal network across product, engineering, and operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with cross-functional teams to align customer needs with product roadmap</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain exceptional customer relationships post-sale to drive expansion opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent Silna at industry events and establish thought leadership</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Business Acumen</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand the healthcare provider landscape and articulate our value proposition</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a deep knowledge of our customers' business challenges and priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on healthcare industry trends, regulations, and competitive offerings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide strategic market intelligence to inform product development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to refining pricing strategies and sales methodologies<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What Sets You Apart</strong></h2><h3><strong>Experience &amp; Skills</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years of proven success in Enterprise Technology Sales, with healthcare technology experience preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistent record of exceeding quota and delivering exceptional results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience navigating complex sales cycles and building relationships with senior executives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills with the ability to articulate complex value propositions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic thinking and deal orchestration capabilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity and the ability to create structure in unstructured environments</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Character &amp; Mindset</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hunger and ambition that drives you to be a top 1% performer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perseverance and resilience in the face of challenges</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Personable and disarming with the ability to build trust quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive edge balanced with collaborative team spirit</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solution-oriented approach to problem-solving</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership mentality and accountability for results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Intrinsic motivation to excel and grow</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About Silna</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why Join Silna</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ground-floor opportunity to shape the sales function at a rapidly growing startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with the founding team and influence company direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation package including equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Chance to make a meaningful impact on healthcare delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fast-paced, dynamic environment that rewards initiative and results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to solve complex problems alongside brilliant colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is perfect for a highly motivated sales professional who wants to be instrumental in building something transformative. If you're ready to join a mission-driven company that's revolutionizing healthcare administration, we want to talk to you.</p><h2></h2><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A rapid-paced work environment with an incredibly enthusiastic and motivated team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The opportunity to work with customers that <em><strong>actually love</strong></em> the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to work on a technology that is materially improving health outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation and benefits package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p><h2></h2></li></ul><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This position is based in our New York City office.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ENTERPRISE ACCOUNT EXECUTIVE AT SILNA https://www.silnahealth.com\n\n\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\nAs Silna experiences explosive growth, we're seeking a top-tier Enterprise Account Executive to join our team in NYC. This is a ground-floor opportunity to shape our enterprise sales function and drive significant impact as we transform how healthcare providers clear patients for care.\n\nReporting directly to the CEO, you'll manage the full sales cycle for enterprise accounts, develop and execute strategic sales plans, and contribute to defining our go-to-market strategy. This role demands someone who thrives in ambiguity, builds exceptional relationships, and approaches sales with strategic sophistication.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n\nSALES EXECUTION & STRATEGY\n\n - Manage the full sales cycle from prospecting to closing enterprise deals\n\n - Develop and execute territory plans to achieve and exceed quota\n\n - Create and deliver compelling presentations tailored to each prospect's unique challenges\n\n - Navigate complex buying committees and build consensus among multiple stakeholders\n\n - Negotiate contracts and strategic partnerships to maximize value\n\n - Identify patterns and opportunities in the market before competitors\n\n\nRELATIONSHIP BUILDING\n\n - Cultivate relationships with C-level executives and key decision makers\n\n - Build a strong internal network across product, engineering, and operations\n\n - Collaborate with cross-functional teams to align customer needs with product roadmap\n\n - Maintain exceptional customer relationships post-sale to drive expansion opportunities\n\n - Represent Silna at industry events and establish thought leadership\n\n\nBUSINESS ACUMEN\n\n - Understand the healthcare provider landscape and articulate our value proposition\n\n - Develop a deep knowledge of our customers' business challenges and priorities\n\n - Stay current on healthcare industry trends, regulations, and competitive offerings\n\n - Provide strategic market intelligence to inform product development\n\n - Contribute to refining pricing strategies and sales methodologies\n   \n\n\nWHAT SETS YOU APART\n\n\nEXPERIENCE & SKILLS\n\n - 3-5 years of proven success in Enterprise Technology Sales, with healthcare technology experience preferred\n\n - Consistent record of exceeding quota and delivering exceptional results\n\n - Experience navigating complex sales cycles and building relationships with senior executives\n\n - Strong communication skills with the ability to articulate complex value propositions\n\n - Strategic thinking and deal orchestration capabilities\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and the ability to create structure in unstructured environments\n\n\nCHARACTER & MINDSET\n\n - Hunger and ambition that drives you to be a top 1% performer\n\n - Perseverance and resilience in the face of challenges\n\n - Personable and disarming with the ability to build trust quickly\n\n - Competitive edge balanced with collaborative team spirit\n\n - Solution-oriented approach to problem-solving\n\n - Ownership mentality and accountability for results\n\n - Intrinsic motivation to excel and grow\n\n\n\n\nABOUT SILNA\n\nHealthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.\n\nSilna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.\n\nWe work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.\n\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN SILNA\n\n - Ground-floor opportunity to shape the sales function at a rapidly growing startup\n\n - Work directly with the founding team and influence company direction\n\n - Competitive compensation package including equity\n\n - Chance to make a meaningful impact on healthcare delivery\n\n - Fast-paced, dynamic environment that rewards initiative and results\n\n - Opportunity to solve complex problems alongside brilliant colleagues\n\nThis role is perfect for a highly motivated sales professional who wants to be instrumental in building something transformative. If you're ready to join a mission-driven company that's revolutionizing healthcare administration, we want to talk to you.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A rapid-paced work environment with an incredibly enthusiastic and motivated team.\n\n - The opportunity to work with customers that actually love the product.\n\n - The ability to work on a technology that is materially improving health outcomes\n\n - Competitive compensation and benefits package\n\n - 401k\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n   \n   \n   \n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis position is based in our New York City office.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $160K • $240-320k OTE","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $160K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0d51478d-3895-431d-90fe-a5aa13f94949","tierSummary":"$120K – $160K • $240-320k OTE","title":null,"additionalInformation":"$240-320k OTE","components":[{"id":"d7039730-2002-4949-ab73-9f39a1ff30b8","summary":"$120K – $160K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000}]}},{"id":"6706f06f-997f-473f-b1cc-62bd11d83be5","title":"Founding Partnerships Lead","department":"GTM","team":"GTM","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"NYC","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-31T15:27:09.664+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/6706f06f-997f-473f-b1cc-62bd11d83be5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/6706f06f-997f-473f-b1cc-62bd11d83be5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Silna</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Silna's first dedicated Partnerships hire, you will build the function from the ground up, identify which channels can compound our reach across the healthcare ecosystem, get the right agreements signed, and lead every partnership from first conversation to measurable, compounding revenue. You own the full cycle. You will cultivate relationships across EHR and practice management vendors, health systems, payer networks, GPOs, and the emerging infrastructure layer of specialty care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will report directly to the CEO with a mandate to transform Silna from a high-growth startup into an industry infrastructure player. The partnerships you build will expand our distribution and shape how the next generation of the healthcare revenue stack is built.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you've spent your career looking for a market that genuinely needed disruption, a product that actually works, and a company early enough that you can still shape it, this is it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source, evaluate, and prioritize net-new partnership opportunities across EHR platforms, RCM companies, referral and intake networks, and adjacent healthcare technology vendors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the full partnership cycle from first conversation through signed agreement through revenue, and be accountable for outcomes, not just activity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a partnerships playbook from zero: develop hypotheses about which partner types convert, test them, and codify what works into repeatable, scalable processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with sales to leverage existing customer relationships as social proof and entry points with potential partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally with product and engineering to shape partnership requirements and ensure Silna can deliver on what you sell</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the infrastructure (pipeline tracking, attribution, performance reporting) that turns a partnerships function into a predictable revenue channel</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent Silna at conferences, partner meetings, and industry events, determining which are worth investment as you go</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Are Looking For</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Either 4+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, or strategic sales roles OR a former founder who has GTM experience who has closed deals and built from nothing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building partnerships at a startup or quickly growing company where you did not have the luxury of brand recognition or an established partner program. You have sold from a position of weakness, not strength</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record that goes beyond logos. You can point to pipeline generated, deals closed, and revenue that moved because of something you built</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with complex, multi-party deal structures and long sales cycles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Systems thinking and strategic judgment: you can evaluate five different partnership profiles, form a clear opinion on which to prioritize, and defend that opinion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with healthcare, insurance, or regulated industries is a plus but not required. You are smart enough to learn the domain quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and professional polish. You will be in rooms with C-suite operators, practice owners, and platform executives</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>This Probably Is Not for You If</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your partnerships experience is primarily at a large enterprise where distribution, brand, and an existing playbook did the heavy lifting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You need a partner marketing team, partner ops team, or solutions engineering support to be effective. This is an IC role where you create your own leverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your experience is mostly non-revenue partnerships: co-marketing, content, or brand collaborations without commercial accountability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are more comfortable managing existing partner relationships than building new ones from scratch</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna is based in New York City. This role is in-person five days a week with travel to partner and customer sites as needed.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT SILNA\n\nHealthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.\n\nSilna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.\n\nWe work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs Silna's first dedicated Partnerships hire, you will build the function from the ground up, identify which channels can compound our reach across the healthcare ecosystem, get the right agreements signed, and lead every partnership from first conversation to measurable, compounding revenue. You own the full cycle. You will cultivate relationships across EHR and practice management vendors, health systems, payer networks, GPOs, and the emerging infrastructure layer of specialty care.\n\nYou will report directly to the CEO with a mandate to transform Silna from a high-growth startup into an industry infrastructure player. The partnerships you build will expand our distribution and shape how the next generation of the healthcare revenue stack is built.\n\nIf you've spent your career looking for a market that genuinely needed disruption, a product that actually works, and a company early enough that you can still shape it, this is it.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Source, evaluate, and prioritize net-new partnership opportunities across EHR platforms, RCM companies, referral and intake networks, and adjacent healthcare technology vendors\n\n - Own the full partnership cycle from first conversation through signed agreement through revenue, and be accountable for outcomes, not just activity\n\n - Build a partnerships playbook from zero: develop hypotheses about which partner types convert, test them, and codify what works into repeatable, scalable processes\n\n - Coordinate with sales to leverage existing customer relationships as social proof and entry points with potential partners\n\n - Work cross-functionally with product and engineering to shape partnership requirements and ensure Silna can deliver on what you sell\n\n - Build the infrastructure (pipeline tracking, attribution, performance reporting) that turns a partnerships function into a predictable revenue channel\n\n - Represent Silna at conferences, partner meetings, and industry events, determining which are worth investment as you go\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Either 4+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, or strategic sales roles OR a former founder who has GTM experience who has closed deals and built from nothing\n\n - Experience building partnerships at a startup or quickly growing company where you did not have the luxury of brand recognition or an established partner program. You have sold from a position of weakness, not strength\n\n - A track record that goes beyond logos. You can point to pipeline generated, deals closed, and revenue that moved because of something you built\n\n - Comfort with complex, multi-party deal structures and long sales cycles\n\n - Systems thinking and strategic judgment: you can evaluate five different partnership profiles, form a clear opinion on which to prioritize, and defend that opinion\n\n - Familiarity with healthcare, insurance, or regulated industries is a plus but not required. You are smart enough to learn the domain quickly\n\n - Strong executive presence and professional polish. You will be in rooms with C-suite operators, practice owners, and platform executives\n   \n   \n\n\nTHIS PROBABLY IS NOT FOR YOU IF\n\n - Your partnerships experience is primarily at a large enterprise where distribution, brand, and an existing playbook did the heavy lifting\n\n - You need a partner marketing team, partner ops team, or solutions engineering support to be effective. This is an IC role where you create your own leverage\n\n - Your experience is mostly non-revenue partnerships: co-marketing, content, or brand collaborations without commercial accountability\n\n - You are more comfortable managing existing partner relationships than building new ones from scratch\n\n\n\nSilna is based in New York City. This role is in-person five days a week with travel to partner and customer sites as needed.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$140K – $210K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$140K - $210K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0940d9f8-78d9-42b4-86ee-d7c253537f26","tierSummary":"$140K – $210K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a5f8990f-d278-4ecd-b35c-a5fce80ecd3d","summary":"$140K – $210K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":140000,"maxValue":210000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":140000,"maxValue":210000}]}},{"id":"35a403dd-34ff-4d72-a6f9-6f8b9594548c","title":"Founding Recruiter","department":"Talent","team":"Talent","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"NYC","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-13T21:55:06.169+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/35a403dd-34ff-4d72-a6f9-6f8b9594548c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/35a403dd-34ff-4d72-a6f9-6f8b9594548c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Silna</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring our first in-house <strong>Recruiter</strong> to own hiring across engineering, go-to-market, and operations. You’ll be both a strategic partner and a hands-on sourcer, building pipelines, closing top talent, and shaping the processes that will scale our team from 30 to 50+ people. In this role, you’ll shape our talent narrative, design scalable processes, and build a brand that consistently attracts top performers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why Join Us</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ground-floor opportunity to build the recruiting function from scratch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mission-driven impact: Help healthcare providers spend more time with patients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unprecedented growth: Series A backed, doubling revenue quarter over quarter</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cutting-edge technology transforming healthcare operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High-visibility role with direct access to the CEO and C-Suite</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative culture: Smart, passionate, in-office team committed to excellence</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Full-Cycle Recruiting Excellence</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the end-to-end recruiting process from sourcing to offer negotiation across all functions and roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage role intake, sourcing, screening, interviewing, closing, and onboarding handoff.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sourcing &amp; Engagement</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actively source top talent through LinkedIn outreach, referrals, events, and creative channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tailor messaging to reflect evolving company needs and inspire interest in Silna.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build deep pipelines for both current and future needs.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stakeholder Partnership</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with hiring managers to deeply understand role requirements, team dynamics, and ideal candidate profiles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide data-driven hiring insights to inform strategy.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Candidate Experience &amp; Talent Brand</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver a best-in-class candidate journey that reinforces our values — even for those we don’t hire.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Position Silna as a destination employer in competitive markets.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process &amp; Systems Building</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Initially focus on sourcing and closing; evolve into building scalable processes, tools, and metrics to reduce reliance on external sources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and report on key metrics using data to support recruitment strategy</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of full-cycle recruiting in high-growth technology companies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success hiring across multiple functions, with strong technical recruiting skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of sourcing and closing passive candidates in competitive markets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building recruiting processes and systems in fast-paced environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data-driven, analytical mindset — uses metrics to optimize strategy and execution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication and stakeholder management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with ATS platforms (Ashby, Greenhouse, etc.) and sourcing tools</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Built recruiting functions from scratch at Series B–D stage companies (under 250 employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in VC-backed SaaS environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in companies that doubled headcount within 18–24 months</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">History of winning top talent from outside well-known employers<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive salary + equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive benefits package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative, high-energy work environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to make a significant impact and define a new market category</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT SILNA\n\nHealthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.\n\nSilna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.\n\nWe work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe’re hiring our first in-house Recruiter to own hiring across engineering, go-to-market, and operations. You’ll be both a strategic partner and a hands-on sourcer, building pipelines, closing top talent, and shaping the processes that will scale our team from 30 to 50+ people. In this role, you’ll shape our talent narrative, design scalable processes, and build a brand that consistently attracts top performers.\n\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN US\n\n - Ground-floor opportunity to build the recruiting function from scratch\n\n - Mission-driven impact: Help healthcare providers spend more time with patients\n\n - Unprecedented growth: Series A backed, doubling revenue quarter over quarter\n\n - Cutting-edge technology transforming healthcare operations\n\n - High-visibility role with direct access to the CEO and C-Suite\n\n - Collaborative culture: Smart, passionate, in-office team committed to excellence\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n\n - Full-Cycle Recruiting Excellence\n   \n   - Own the end-to-end recruiting process from sourcing to offer negotiation across all functions and roles.\n   \n   - Manage role intake, sourcing, screening, interviewing, closing, and onboarding handoff.\n\n - Sourcing & Engagement\n   \n   - Actively source top talent through LinkedIn outreach, referrals, events, and creative channels.\n   \n   - Tailor messaging to reflect evolving company needs and inspire interest in Silna.\n   \n   - Build deep pipelines for both current and future needs.\n\n - Stakeholder Partnership\n   \n   - Collaborate with hiring managers to deeply understand role requirements, team dynamics, and ideal candidate profiles.\n   \n   - Provide data-driven hiring insights to inform strategy.\n\n - Candidate Experience & Talent Brand\n   \n   - Deliver a best-in-class candidate journey that reinforces our values — even for those we don’t hire.\n   \n   - Position Silna as a destination employer in competitive markets.\n\n - Process & Systems Building\n   \n   - Initially focus on sourcing and closing; evolve into building scalable processes, tools, and metrics to reduce reliance on external sources\n   \n   - Track and report on key metrics using data to support recruitment strategy\n\n\n\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - 4+ years of full-cycle recruiting in high-growth technology companies\n\n - Proven success hiring across multiple functions, with strong technical recruiting skills\n\n - Track record of sourcing and closing passive candidates in competitive markets\n\n - Experience building recruiting processes and systems in fast-paced environments\n\n - Data-driven, analytical mindset — uses metrics to optimize strategy and execution\n\n - Exceptional communication and stakeholder management skills\n\n - Proficiency with ATS platforms (Ashby, Greenhouse, etc.) and sourcing tools\n\n\n\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Built recruiting functions from scratch at Series B–D stage companies (under 250 employees)\n\n - Experience in VC-backed SaaS environments\n\n - Background in companies that doubled headcount within 18–24 months\n\n - History of winning top talent from outside well-known employers\n   \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Competitive salary + equity\n\n - Comprehensive benefits package\n\n - 401(k)\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n - Collaborative, high-energy work environment\n\n - Opportunity to make a significant impact and define a new market category","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"28ba5d0b-b862-4e04-995d-d5eff22d269e","title":"AI Deployment Analyst","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"NYC","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-17T13:31:58.222+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/28ba5d0b-b862-4e04-995d-d5eff22d269e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/28ba5d0b-b862-4e04-995d-d5eff22d269e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>AI Deployment Analyst at Silna</strong></h2><h3><strong>About the Role:</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a curious, analytical teammate to join our AI Operations team at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.silnahealth.com\">Silna</a>. In this role, you’ll help us design, test, and roll out AI deployments that interpret complex healthcare documents, like treatment plans and prior authorization approval letters, using optical character recognition (OCR) and agentic AI. You will work on the end-to-end deployment of browser and phone agents for automating healthcare web-based workflows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a great role for a recent graduate with a background in computer science, data science, or a non-technical field who wants to apply those skills in a real-world, high-impact healthcare setting. You’ll work closely with operations and engineering to make sure our AI systems produce accurate, usable outputs that enable patients to access care faster.</p><h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop, test, and refine AI deployments that extract structured information from healthcare documents (e.g., treatment plans, prior authorization approvals) or web-based authorization and verification workflows. Analyze model outputs for accuracy and identify areas for improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with operations and engineering teams to translate healthcare and insurance workflows into clear technical specifications for AI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create documentation and playbooks to ensure prompt strategies are reproducible and scalable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay up-to-date with best practices in AI prompting, document parsing, and healthcare data handling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross functionally with our team of healthcare experts to drive the roll out of our automation strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Measure and evaluate progress by creating clearly defined metrics.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Qualifications</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> Background in computer science, data science, or non-technical field but with strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities (recent graduates encouraged to apply).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in natural language processing concepts, AI/ML, or OCR technologies (coursework or internship experience counts!).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think critically about ambiguous problems and propose structured solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus:</strong> Experience with Python, SQL, or healthcare data/insurance workflows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About Silna</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>What We Offer</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A fast-paced work environment with an incredibly enthusiastic and motivated team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The opportunity to work with customers that really love the product</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to work on technology that is materially improving health outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation and benefits package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"AI DEPLOYMENT ANALYST AT SILNA\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE:\n\nWe are looking for a curious, analytical teammate to join our AI Operations team at Silna https://www.silnahealth.com. In this role, you’ll help us design, test, and roll out AI deployments that interpret complex healthcare documents, like treatment plans and prior authorization approval letters, using optical character recognition (OCR) and agentic AI. You will work on the end-to-end deployment of browser and phone agents for automating healthcare web-based workflows.\n\nThis is a great role for a recent graduate with a background in computer science, data science, or a non-technical field who wants to apply those skills in a real-world, high-impact healthcare setting. You’ll work closely with operations and engineering to make sure our AI systems produce accurate, usable outputs that enable patients to access care faster.\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Develop, test, and refine AI deployments that extract structured information from healthcare documents (e.g., treatment plans, prior authorization approvals) or web-based authorization and verification workflows. Analyze model outputs for accuracy and identify areas for improvement.\n\n - Work with operations and engineering teams to translate healthcare and insurance workflows into clear technical specifications for AI.\n\n - Create documentation and playbooks to ensure prompt strategies are reproducible and scalable.\n\n - Stay up-to-date with best practices in AI prompting, document parsing, and healthcare data handling.\n\n - Work cross functionally with our team of healthcare experts to drive the roll out of our automation strategies.\n\n - Measure and evaluate progress by creating clearly defined metrics.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n -  Background in computer science, data science, or non-technical field but with strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities (recent graduates encouraged to apply).\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with attention to detail.\n\n - Interest in natural language processing concepts, AI/ML, or OCR technologies (coursework or internship experience counts!).\n\n - Ability to think critically about ambiguous problems and propose structured solutions.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills.\n\n - Bonus: Experience with Python, SQL, or healthcare data/insurance workflows.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT SILNA\n\nHealthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.\n\nSilna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.\n\nWe work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - A fast-paced work environment with an incredibly enthusiastic and motivated team\n\n - The opportunity to work with customers that really love the product\n\n - The ability to work on technology that is materially improving health outcomes\n\n - Competitive compensation and benefits package\n\n - 401k\n\n - Unlimited PTO","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $160K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $160K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d8edec54-135f-40ce-b2e6-b3f5a5de0ab1","tierSummary":"$120K – $160K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f55c1e84-507c-49bc-beb6-ab77c3677d61","summary":"$120K – $160K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000}]}},{"id":"22ec4b1c-9807-4d0c-8669-e60767824b05","title":"SDR","department":"GTM","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"NYC","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-01T16:36:58.948+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/22ec4b1c-9807-4d0c-8669-e60767824b05","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/22ec4b1c-9807-4d0c-8669-e60767824b05/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Sales Development Representative</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About Silna</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Silna experiences explosive growth, we're seeking a hungry and driven Sales Development Representative to join our team in NYC. This is a ground-floor opportunity to build our lead generation engine and be the foundation of our sales success as we transform how healthcare providers clear patients for care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting directly to our Account Executive, you'll own the top of our sales funnel, develop and execute prospecting strategies, and contribute to defining our lead qualification process. This role demands someone who thrives on the grind, obsesses over continuous improvement, and approaches each day with relentless energy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Prospecting &amp; Lead generation</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute multi-channel outreach campaigns (email, phone, LinkedIn, events)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and identify ideal customer profiles across clinics, practices, and health systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain comprehensive prospect databases using CRM and sales intelligence tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generate qualified meetings and demos for the Account Executive team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pipeline Development</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualify prospects based on fit, need, and buying authority</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nurture leads through strategic follow-up sequences until ready for handoff</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and optimize key metrics: calls made, emails sent, meetings scheduled, conversion rates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with marketing to refine messaging and campaign effectiveness</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Process Building &amp; Optimization</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and refine SDR playbooks, scripts, and qualification frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Test new prospecting channels and techniques to improve results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze what's working and iterate on approaches daily</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create templates and workflows that can scale with team growth</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Market Intelligence</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on healthcare industry trends and pain points</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research competitor solutions and positioning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide feedback on prospect objections and market insights</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What Sets You Apart</strong></h2><h2><strong>Experience &amp; Skills</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year in sales development, lead generation, or high-activity sales roles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of consistently hitting or exceeding quota</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills with healthcare professionals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to articulate value propositions clearly and compellingly</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Character &amp; Mindset</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relentless hunger and drive to be a top performer every single day</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Growth obsession - constantly seeking ways to improve performance and learn new skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resilience and grit - thrives on overcoming rejection and obstacles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process-oriented - disciplined about tracking activities and optimizing approaches</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership mentality - takes full accountability for results and pipeline contribution</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is perfect for someone who wakes up every morning ready to outwork yesterday's version of themselves. If you're obsessed with the grind, hungry for growth, and want to be instrumental in building something transformative in healthcare, we want to talk to you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A rapid-paced work environment with an incredibly enthusiastic and motivated team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The opportunity to work with customers that <em><strong>actually love</strong></em> the product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to work on a technology that is materially improving health outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation and benefits package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This position is based either in our New York City office or remote.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"SALES DEVELOPMENT REPRESENTATIVE\n\n\n\n\nABOUT SILNA\n\nHealthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.\n\nSilna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.\n\nWe work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.\n\n\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\nAs Silna experiences explosive growth, we're seeking a hungry and driven Sales Development Representative to join our team in NYC. This is a ground-floor opportunity to build our lead generation engine and be the foundation of our sales success as we transform how healthcare providers clear patients for care.\n\n\n\nReporting directly to our Account Executive, you'll own the top of our sales funnel, develop and execute prospecting strategies, and contribute to defining our lead qualification process. This role demands someone who thrives on the grind, obsesses over continuous improvement, and approaches each day with relentless energy.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\nProspecting & Lead generation\n\n - Execute multi-channel outreach campaigns (email, phone, LinkedIn, events)\n\n - Research and identify ideal customer profiles across clinics, practices, and health systems\n\n - Build and maintain comprehensive prospect databases using CRM and sales intelligence tools\n\n - Generate qualified meetings and demos for the Account Executive team\n\nPipeline Development\n\n - Qualify prospects based on fit, need, and buying authority\n\n - Nurture leads through strategic follow-up sequences until ready for handoff\n\n - Track and optimize key metrics: calls made, emails sent, meetings scheduled, conversion rates\n\n - Collaborate with marketing to refine messaging and campaign effectiveness\n\nProcess Building & Optimization\n\n - Develop and refine SDR playbooks, scripts, and qualification frameworks\n\n - Test new prospecting channels and techniques to improve results\n\n - Analyze what's working and iterate on approaches daily\n\n - Create templates and workflows that can scale with team growth\n\nMarket Intelligence\n\n - Stay current on healthcare industry trends and pain points\n\n - Research competitor solutions and positioning\n\n - Provide feedback on prospect objections and market insights\n\n\n\n\nWHAT SETS YOU APART\n\n\nEXPERIENCE & SKILLS\n\n - 1+ year in sales development, lead generation, or high-activity sales roles\n\n - Proven track record of consistently hitting or exceeding quota\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills with healthcare professionals\n\n - Ability to articulate value propositions clearly and compellingly\n\n\nCHARACTER & MINDSET\n\n - Relentless hunger and drive to be a top performer every single day\n\n - Growth obsession - constantly seeking ways to improve performance and learn new skills\n\n - Resilience and grit - thrives on overcoming rejection and obstacles\n\n - Process-oriented - disciplined about tracking activities and optimizing approaches\n\n - Ownership mentality - takes full accountability for results and pipeline contribution\n\nThis role is perfect for someone who wakes up every morning ready to outwork yesterday's version of themselves. If you're obsessed with the grind, hungry for growth, and want to be instrumental in building something transformative in healthcare, we want to talk to you.\n\n\n\nWhat We Offer\n\n - A rapid-paced work environment with an incredibly enthusiastic and motivated team.\n\n - The opportunity to work with customers that actually love the product.\n\n - The ability to work on a technology that is materially improving health outcomes\n\n - Competitive compensation and benefits package\n\n - 401k\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n   \n   \n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis position is based either in our New York City office or remote.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$60K – $100K • 100-125k OTE","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$60K - $100K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"65cbb03a-e602-4f1e-bc6b-a99a309a82ca","tierSummary":"$60K – $100K • 100-125k OTE","title":null,"additionalInformation":"100-125k OTE","components":[{"id":"d9a501cc-6cd7-484e-9e9a-56b4361e795b","summary":"$60K – $100K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":60000,"maxValue":100000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":60000,"maxValue":100000}]}},{"id":"ac1333f5-88e0-4809-9e46-a4671961939a","title":"Payor Process & Documentation Specialist","department":"Operations Specialists","team":"Operations Specialists","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T14:15:29.156+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/ac1333f5-88e0-4809-9e46-a4671961939a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/silnahealth.com/ac1333f5-88e0-4809-9e46-a4671961939a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About the Position</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a meticulous technical writer with foundational knowledge of revenue cycle management, particularly prior authorization, to turn complex, ever-changing payor requirements into clear, standardized documentation our team can rely on. This role is primarily about writing: producing and maintaining checklists, requirement guides, and process documentation that are accurate, consistently formatted, and easy for anyone on the team to follow. A smaller part of the role (roughly a quarter to a third of your time) involves original research into payor-specific submission processes to keep that documentation current.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be successful here if you have a track record of producing polished, standardized work with very few errors; where mistakes do happen, they show up in edge cases rather than in the foundational facts. We need someone who treats documentation as a craft: consistent terminology, consistent structure, and zero ambiguity for the reader.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Documentation, Annotation, &amp; Checklist Creation</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write and maintain clear, standardized documentation of payor requirements, submission processes, and authorization workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and refine checklists for prior authorization and benefit verification submissions across payors, ensuring consistent format and terminology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annotate and tag source materials (payor policies, portal captures, requirement documents) with structured, consistent labels for internal reference and systems use</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Edit and standardize documentation drafted by others so all materials follow a consistent style, structure, and level of detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep documentation current as payor policies change, with clear version tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proofread and quality-check all documentation for accuracy, consistency, and clarity before it goes live</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and validate prior authorization and benefit verification requirements across diverse payors (commercial plans, state Medicaid programs, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate payor-specific submission processes (required documents, portals, fax numbers, CPT code requirements) when existing documentation is unclear, outdated, or missing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate information from multiple sources and assess the credibility of payor guidance before it's documented<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foundational knowledge of revenue cycle management (RCM), with specific familiarity with prior authorization processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical writing skills; demonstrated ability to produce clear, structured, standardized documentation (writing samples or a portfolio a plus)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of accurate, low-error output, where any errors tend to occur in non-foundational details rather than core facts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience creating checklists, SOPs, style guides, or other standardized reference materials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort annotating or tagging structured content for documentation or data systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid research skills and comfort navigating payor portals, websites, and policy documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and bring structure to ambiguous or undocumented processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written communication skills and comfort incorporating feedback</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About Silna</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Silna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Why Join Silna</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ground-floor opportunity to build foundational operations at a rapidly growing startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with the founding team and influence company direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation package including equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Chance to make a meaningful impact on healthcare delivery through operational excellence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fast-paced, dynamic environment that rewards initiative and results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to solve complex problems alongside brilliant colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is perfect for someone who loves building systems from scratch, thrives in fast-paced environments, and wants to be instrumental in transforming how healthcare providers interact with insurance. If you're ready to join a mission-driven company that's revolutionizing healthcare administration through operational excellence, we want to talk to you.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT THE POSITION\n\nWe're looking for a meticulous technical writer with foundational knowledge of revenue cycle management, particularly prior authorization, to turn complex, ever-changing payor requirements into clear, standardized documentation our team can rely on. This role is primarily about writing: producing and maintaining checklists, requirement guides, and process documentation that are accurate, consistently formatted, and easy for anyone on the team to follow. A smaller part of the role (roughly a quarter to a third of your time) involves original research into payor-specific submission processes to keep that documentation current.\n\n\n\nYou'll be successful here if you have a track record of producing polished, standardized work with very few errors; where mistakes do happen, they show up in edge cases rather than in the foundational facts. We need someone who treats documentation as a craft: consistent terminology, consistent structure, and zero ambiguity for the reader.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\nDocumentation, Annotation, & Checklist Creation\n\n - Write and maintain clear, standardized documentation of payor requirements, submission processes, and authorization workflows\n\n - Build and refine checklists for prior authorization and benefit verification submissions across payors, ensuring consistent format and terminology\n\n - Annotate and tag source materials (payor policies, portal captures, requirement documents) with structured, consistent labels for internal reference and systems use\n\n - Edit and standardize documentation drafted by others so all materials follow a consistent style, structure, and level of detail\n\n - Keep documentation current as payor policies change, with clear version tracking\n\n - Proofread and quality-check all documentation for accuracy, consistency, and clarity before it goes live\n\n\n\nResearch\n\n - Research and validate prior authorization and benefit verification requirements across diverse payors (commercial plans, state Medicaid programs, etc.)\n\n - Investigate payor-specific submission processes (required documents, portals, fax numbers, CPT code requirements) when existing documentation is unclear, outdated, or missing\n\n - Validate information from multiple sources and assess the credibility of payor guidance before it's documented\n   \n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - Foundational knowledge of revenue cycle management (RCM), with specific familiarity with prior authorization processes\n\n - Strong technical writing skills; demonstrated ability to produce clear, structured, standardized documentation (writing samples or a portfolio a plus)\n\n - A track record of accurate, low-error output, where any errors tend to occur in non-foundational details rather than core facts\n\n - Experience creating checklists, SOPs, style guides, or other standardized reference materials\n\n - Comfort annotating or tagging structured content for documentation or data systems\n\n - Solid research skills and comfort navigating payor portals, websites, and policy documentation\n\n - Exceptional attention to detail\n\n - Ability to work independently and bring structure to ambiguous or undocumented processes\n\n - Strong written communication skills and comfort incorporating feedback\n\n\n\n\nABOUT SILNA\n\nHealthcare is obsessed with optimizing a broken system. We're making sure it never breaks.\n\nSilna Health attacks the root cause of denied claims: the fragmented, incompatible systems that govern prior authorizations, eligibility verification, and benefit checks, turning workflows that used to take days into decisions made in minutes, before care is ever delivered.\n\nWe work across behavioral health, physical health, ambulatory care, and post-acute care, where administrative failure doesn't just cost money; it can delay or deny patient access entirely. We're backed by Accel and Bain Capital Ventures, and we're building fast.\n\n \n\n\nWHY JOIN SILNA\n\n - Ground-floor opportunity to build foundational operations at a rapidly growing startup\n\n - Work directly with the founding team and influence company direction\n\n - Competitive compensation package including equity\n\n - Chance to make a meaningful impact on healthcare delivery through operational excellence\n\n - Fast-paced, dynamic environment that rewards initiative and results\n\n - Opportunity to solve complex problems alongside brilliant colleagues\n\nThis role is perfect for someone who loves building systems from scratch, thrives in fast-paced environments, and wants to be instrumental in transforming how healthcare providers interact with insurance. If you're ready to join a mission-driven company that's revolutionizing healthcare administration through operational excellence, we want to talk to you.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$30 – $35 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"c9991fda-a296-4705-9fc3-f810673d5c2b","tierSummary":"$30 – $35 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b11932fd-94fb-4f57-aefc-7cce64b07bec","summary":"$30 – $35 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":30,"maxValue":35}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":30,"maxValue":35}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}